WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.097
The leading sparsification method, Deep Gradient
Compression,

00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:09.713
selects gradients above an estimated threshold,
which is an approximate operation.

00:00:09.793 --> 00:00:16.013
But to place those gradients into memory without
conflicts it relies on parallel prefix sum,

00:00:16.093 --> 00:00:19.711
an exact algorithm that builds a balanced binary tree,

00:00:19.791 --> 00:00:22.245
runs in logarithmic sequential steps,

00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:27.381
and touches memory about seven times more than the
theoretical lower bound.

00:00:27.461 --> 00:00:35.050
The authors call this an exact-approximate
mismatch: since only an approximate set of top gradients is required,

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.570
using an expensive exact algorithm to place them is
wasted effort.
